{
  "_comment": [
    "The SDK's coverage decision for every Project-accessible route.",
    "",
    "This file exists to stop ONE specific kind of silent drift: a route added to",
    "the server's authorization registry as project-accessible, shipped, and never",
    "considered from the SDK's side. Nothing would fail. The capability would",
    "simply be invisible to every Go consumer, indefinitely, and nobody would find",
    "out until a developer asked why they had to write raw HTTP for it.",
    "",
    "So it is a gate rather than documentation, checked from BOTH sides:",
    "",
    "  internal/authz/sdk_coverage_test.go  every scoped route in the registry has",
    "                                       an entry here, with the scope the",
    "                                       registry actually enforces, and every",
    "                                       entry names a route that exists and is",
    "                                       documented in the OpenAPI spec.",
    "",
    "  sdk/go/coverage_test.go              every entry marked `supported` names a",
    "                                       method this package really exports, and",
    "                                       that method's doc comment states the",
    "                                       required scope.",
    "",
    "It is JSON, and not Go, precisely because the two checkers are in two",
    "different modules. The SDK module cannot be imported by the server module",
    "without undoing the boundary this slice exists to create, so the shared fact",
    "has to live in something both can read without importing either.",
    "",
    "`status` is `supported` or `unsupported`. `unsupported` REQUIRES a `reason`:",
    "an omission somebody argued for is a decision, an omission nobody wrote down",
    "is an oversight, and the gate cannot tell them apart on its own.",
    "",
    "Operator-only routes are deliberately absent. They are not project-accessible,",
    "so they are not this SDK's to classify — the registry has already refused",
    "them to every credential that could exist."
  ],

  "routes": [
    {
      "method": "GET",
